{
  "id": "primary-auditory-cortex",
  "term": "primary auditory cortex",
  "definition": "The primary auditory cortex is a hearing-related brain area in which neurons are arranged in an ordered map of sound-processing properties. In the cat, it contains distinct modules of narrowly tuned and broadly tuned neurons that differ in how they respond to the spectral and temporal features of sounds.",
